@{
    Layout = "/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

@section HeaderImage
{
    <div class="headerImage2">
        <img src="~/images/CV_Creation.png" />
    </div>
}

<div class="hometext">

    <ul class="ulBreadcrumb" style="padding-top:10px;">
        <li><a href="/">Home <span class="fa fa-angle-right"></span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/home/Greenjob_Midcareer">Mid Career Professional </a></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="bgMidCareerStep1Up2" style="margin-top:-90px"></div>

    <img src="~/images/Fear_of_Being_skipped.png" width="100%" />
    <div class="bgMidCareerStep1lower">
        <p class="paraCommon paraHeader">
            <b>FEAR OF BEING SKIPPED; When Your Career Starts Feeling Like an OTT Ad</b>
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"> Every OTT viewer knows the joy of hitting “Skip Ad.” But what mid-career professionals don’t realize is this:<b> Workplaces are doing the same thing to people.</b> Quietly. Quickly. Without announcement.</p>
        <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
        <p class="paraHeader">1. When Careers Go into Fast-Forward Mode </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Early professionals want everything yesterday. They skip the grind, skip the basics, skip the boring parts, believing the “real career” starts only after the skip button. </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">But this creates a new workplace reality: <b>Organizations have stopped waiting for people to learn.</b> They simply <b>skip</b> whoever is slow, complacent, unskilled, outdated, or stuck in old roles. </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">And unfortunately, the group that experiences this the hardest? <b>Mid-career professionals.</b> </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
        <p class="paraHeader">2. Being Skipped Hurts More When You Don't See It Coming </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">
            In your twenties you skip fundamentals. In your thirties and forties, fundamentals skip you. Suddenly:
            <ul>
                <li>promotions skip you,</li>
                <li>new opportunities skip you,</li>
                <li>strategic conversations skip you,</li>
                <li>projects go to younger, faster, cheaper employees,</li>
                <li>and technology skips your entire job description.</li>
            </ul>
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">You’re still in the room… but the room has stopped noticing. This is the moment mid-career anxiety explodes. </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
        <p class="paraHeader">3. Skipping Is the New Workplace Disease </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Your base draft says it perfectly: “Employees skip depth, founders skip structure, managers skip feedback.” </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">But the real twist is this: <b>Corporates skip mid-career people who don’t grow.</b> </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">
            Not out of cruelty but out of speed. The modern economy rewards:
            <ul>
                <li>adaptability</li>
                <li>continuous learning</li>
                <li>experimentation</li>
                <li>digital fluency</li>
                <li>curiosity</li>
            </ul>
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Mid-career professionals who stay in comfort zones get silently fast-forwarded. </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
        <p class="paraHeader">4. AI Has Made Skipping Even Easier </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">
            AI doesn’t complain. <br />
            AI doesn’t negotiate salary.<br />
            AI doesn’t take leave.<br />
            AI doesn’t need motivation.<br />
            AI doesn’t need patience to master fundamentals — it is the fundamentals.<br />
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">So what happens? Routine mid-career roles get skipped automatically.  </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">
            Storytelling? Automated.<br />
            Reporting? Automated.<br />
            Analysis? Semi-automated.<br />
            Decision-support? AI-assisted.<br />
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">If your work can be skipped, unfortunately… <b>so can you.</b> </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
        <p class="paraHeader">5. The Green Economy Is the Only Sector That Doesn’t Skip Mid-Career Talent </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">
            This is where the magic begins. Green sectors like climate tech, waste-to-value, regenerative agriculture, circular economy, clean mobility, impact enterprises do <b>not</b> function on the “skip culture.” Why? Because these industries need:
            <ul>
                <li>depth</li>
                <li>experience</li>
                <li>maturity</li>
                <li>judgment</li>
                <li>cross-functional understanding</li>
                <li>people who’ve seen cycles of failure and recovery</li>
            </ul>
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Green companies cannot skip these qualities, they depend on them. <b>This is why mid-career professionals are gold here.</b> </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
        <p class="paraHeader">6. Mastery Cannot Be Skipped — Reinvention Cannot Be Rushed </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">
            This is the emotional crux: If you don’t build depth in your thirties and forties, your career becomes skippable. If you don’t reinvent, the industry will reinvent without you. But when you move into the Green Economy, you become unskippable because:
            <ul>
                <li>you bring lived experience </li>
                <li>you understand systems </li>
                <li>you make real-world decisions </li>
                <li>you stabilize teams </li>
                <li>you mentor younger talent </li>
                <li>you help scale operations </li>
                <li>you bring patience for meaningful work </li>
            </ul>
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Green is the opposite of OTT culture, it values slow, deep, real progress. </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
        <p class="paraHeader">7. FINAL TAKEAWAY </p>
        <p class="paraCommon"><b>If you fear being skipped, don’t run faster — switch tracks.</b>  The Green Economy doesn’t skip people. It absorbs them. Respects them. Depends on them. </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">And most importantly - it gives mid-career professionals something that OTT can never offer:<b>  a role that cannot be fast-forwarded. </b> </p>
      
        <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
    </div>
</div>

